# Input
```
-- The parameters of a SQL function are not columns.
-- expect_lint/requireColumnQualifier
create function public.user_name(user_id integer) returns pg_catalog.text
language sql security definer set search_path = ''
as $$ select u.name from public.users u where u.id = user_id and active $$;

```

# Diagnostics
lint/requireColumnQualifier ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × Column active is not qualified with its table.
  
  i Without a table, the column is looked up in every relation of the query and of the queries around it, so a column with the same name in another relation can take its place.
  
  i Qualify the column with the name or alias of its table, e.g. t.active.
